# screen-snip-manager (Clipboard Manager)

macOS 14+ menu bar app keeping a local, searchable clipboard history (text and images, fuzzy search, pins, tags, sensitive-data expiry). `CLAUDE.md` has the architecture, key files and conventions; read it and `README.md` first.

## Stack and local commands (Xcode 15+, macOS)
- Open `ClipboardManager.xcodeproj`, scheme `ClipboardManager` (GRDB via Swift Package Manager).
- Build: `xcodebuild -project "ClipboardManager.xcodeproj" -scheme "ClipboardManager" -configuration Debug build`
- Test: `xcodebuild test -project "ClipboardManager.xcodeproj" -scheme "ClipboardManager" -destination "platform=macOS"` (tests in `ClipboardManagerTests/`; CI runs this in `macos-tests.yml`). CLAUDE.md's "no test target" note is out of date.
- `scripts/build-and-install.sh` installs into /Applications: only on a machine you're told to use.

## Releases: never
- Distribution is a signed/notarized archive or DMG (`scripts/create-dmg.sh`). Agents must never sign, notarize, publish releases or upload builds. Releases, merges and any account or signing change need potac's explicit OK.

## Branches and PRs
- Default branch `main`. Never push to it. Small, focused draft PRs; never merge or close PRs. Keep CI (macOS tests, CodeQL) green.

## How to work
- Reproduce a bug before fixing it (a failing test first where possible). Reuse and delete before adding.
- Keep clipboard data local: no network calls, telemetry or logging of clipboard contents. Settings go through `UserDefaultsKeys.swift`.
- Never commit secrets or print them (signing identities, team IDs, notary credentials).
- No personal names in code, docs or commits.
